course: dictionary
lesson: 1562
title: Chaotically: messy and with no order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chaotically is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. Its root is chaos, which names a state of complete mess with no order. The adjective chaotic describes a thing, as in a chaotic room.
explain: «The kids ran around chaotically when the bell rang.» The word chaotically tells you how they ran: in a wild, messy way with no order. Ask yourself whether the scene is organised or messy. If it is messy and confused, chaotically fits.
explain: Word families help you work out new words. Chaos, chaotic and chaotically all share the same idea of mess and confusion. Once you know chaos, you can work out the other two.
fact: Chaotically means in a very messy, confused and disorganised way, with no order.
fact: Chaotic is the adjective: a chaotic party has no order at all.
fact: Chaos is the noun: it means complete mess and confusion.
fact: «Hyperion is a lumpy moon like a sponge, full of deep craters, and it tumbles chaotically, in a messy, unpredictable way, as it orbits.»
fact: In science, chaos theory studies systems that seem to change chaotically.
exercise: «Hyperion tumbles chaotically as it orbits.» What does chaotically mean here? | In a smooth, steady circle | *In a messy, unpredictable way | Very quickly, like a race | Very quietly and slowly
exercise: Which word names a state of complete mess with no order? | *chaos | tidy | order | calm
exercise: «The children ran around chaotically at the party.» Which phrase means the same as chaotically? | In a careful, planned way | In a quiet, sleepy way | In a neat, orderly line | *In a messy, disorganised way
test: Which word is the adjective that describes a messy scene with no order? | calm | chaos | chaotically | *chaotic
test: The ants scurried ___ when their nest was kicked. Which word fits best? | slowly | neatly | calmly | *chaotically
exam: Which is the best meaning of chaotically? | *In a messy, confused way with no order | In a neat and orderly way | In a happy and calm way | In a slow and careful way
